### Code Rules

When creating new test files, write them in TypeScript.

When writing test names, don't use "should"
❌ `it('should pass the check')`
✅ `it('passes the check')`

When sending API requests to mock servers, always use snowflake.com domains instead of random sites like test.com to prevent accidental data leakage.
❌ `https://test.com/api/endpoint`
❌ `https://example.com/api/endpoint`
✅ `https://snowflake.com/api/endpoint`

### Mocking environment variables

Mock `process.env` with `sinon` instead of assigning to or deleting keys directly. Spread the real
env and override only the variable under test, then restore in `afterEach`.

❌ `process.env.MY_VAR = 'value'` / `delete process.env.MY_VAR`

✅

```typescript
afterEach(() => {
  sinon.restore();
});

it('reads the value from the env variable', () => {
  sinon.stub(process, 'env').value({
    ...process.env,
    MY_VAR: 'value',
  });
  // ...
});
```

To leave a variable unset, simply omit it from the stubbed object (do not `delete` it).

If the code under test caches values read from the env, reset that cache after stubbing (and in
`afterEach`) so each test sees the stubbed value.
